    {day:1,title:"Which traits do horses and zebras inherit?",short:"Inherited Traits",image:"assets/science-winter-migration-v1.png",icon:"🦓",reward:"Trait Comparison Card",rewardIcon:"🗂️",story:"Horses and zebras inherit physical and behavioral traits from their parents. A zebra's stripes are physical, while a horse's gentle nature is behavioral. Horses are usually easier to ride, but zebras tolerate heat and drought and resist some diseases better.",guide:"Darwin",guideLine:"Classify each characteristic as physical or behavioral before comparing the animals.",words:[word("inherited trait","đặc điểm di truyền","a physical or behavioral characteristic passed from parent to offspring","noun phrase","A zebra's stripes are an inherited trait."),word("physical trait","đặc điểm thể chất","an inherited feature of an organism's body","noun phrase","Coat color is a physical trait."),word("behavioral trait","đặc điểm hành vi","an inherited or learned pattern of action","noun phrase","A calm nature can be a behavioral trait.")],questions:[matching("Classify each example.",[{left:"zebra stripes",right:"physical trait"},{left:"horse body shape",right:"physical trait"},{left:"gentle nature",right:"behavioral trait"}],"Traits can describe either body features or patterns of behavior.","Visible body patterns are physical.","Nature or temperament describes behavior."),mcq("Which zebra trait can be useful in a hot, dry region?",["Tolerance of heat and drought","A shape comfortable for a saddle","Easy domestication"],0,"Zebras are sturdy and tolerate hot, dry conditions.","Compare environmental tolerance.","The useful trait concerns climate."),tf("Test the heredity claim.","Inherited traits can include both body features and behaviors.",true,"Parents can pass physical and behavioral characteristics to offspring.","Traits are not limited to appearance.","The lesson gives examples of both types.")]},
    {day:2,title:"How are genus and species different?",short:"Classification",image:"assets/science-winter-migration-v1.png",icon:"🏷️",reward:"Genus-Species Key",rewardIcon:"🗝️",story:"Scientists classify organisms by shared inherited traits. Horses and zebras share enough major traits to belong to the same genus, but they are different species. Members of one species can normally reproduce with one another and produce fertile offspring.",guide:"Darwin",guideLine:"A genus may hold several related species; a species is the more specific group.",words:[word("fertile","có khả năng sinh sản","able to reproduce","adjective","Fertile offspring can later produce young."),word("genus","chi","a group of closely related species sharing major traits","noun","Horses and zebras belong to the same genus."),word("species","loài","a type of organism whose members can reproduce with one another","noun","All domestic horses belong to one species.")],questions:[matching("Match each classification term.",[{left:"genus",right:"group of closely related species"},{left:"species",right:"organisms that can produce fertile offspring together"},{left:"fertile",right:"able to reproduce"}],"The terms move from a broad related group to reproductive ability.","A genus contains species.","Fertile describes offspring that can reproduce."),tf("Test the grouping claim.","Organisms in the same genus must always belong to the same species.",false,"A genus can contain several distinct but closely related species.","One genus can have multiple branches.","Horse and zebra show the difference."),mcq("What is the strongest evidence that two organisms belong to the same species?",["They can produce fertile offspring together","They are approximately the same size","They live on the same continent"],0,"Reproduction producing fertile offspring is the key species criterion in this lesson.","Focus on reproduction.","The offspring must also be able to reproduce.")]},
    {day:3,title:"What is a hybrid?",short:"Zebroid Traits",image:"assets/science-winter-migration-v1.png",icon:"🐴",reward:"Hybrid Trait Atlas",rewardIcon:"🧬",story:"Closely related animals from different species sometimes reproduce. Their offspring is a hybrid. A zebroid inherits a mixture of traits from a horse and a zebra: its body may resemble a horse, while stripes, a spiky mane or disease resistance may come from the zebra.",guide:"Darwin",guideLine:"Every hybrid trait must be traced to one of its two parents.",words:[word("hybrid","con lai","the offspring of parents from different species","noun","A zebroid is a horse-zebra hybrid."),word("offspring","con non","a new organism produced by parent organisms","noun","The offspring inherits traits from both parents."),word("unpredictable","khó dự đoán","not certain or easy to forecast","adjective","A hybrid's exact appearance can be unpredictable.")],questions:[mcq("Why does a zebroid show both horse and zebra traits?",["It inherits genes from two different parent species","It changes species every day","Its stripes are painted on"],0,"A hybrid receives inherited information from each parent.","Use the definition of hybrid.","Each parent contributes traits."),matching("Match each likely zebroid feature to its source.",[{left:"striped coat",right:"zebra parent"},{left:"horse-like body",right:"horse parent"},{left:"mixed appearance",right:"inheritance from both parents"}],"A zebroid combines traits from both species.","Stripes identify the zebra contribution.","The overall mixture comes from both."),tf("Test the parent claim.","A hybrid is produced by two parents from the same species only.",false,"A hybrid results from parents belonging to different species.","Recall the defining difference.","Different species is essential here.")]},
    {day:4,title:"Why are many zebroids sterile?",short:"Hybrid Limits",image:"assets/science-winter-migration-v1.png",icon:"⚖️",reward:"Hybrid Evidence Report",rewardIcon:"📊",story:"Zebroids can combine useful traits for hot, dry regions, but many are sterile and cannot produce offspring. Hybrids may also differ greatly from one another because their trait combinations are unpredictable. These benefits and limits are part of the debate about deliberately breeding hybrids.",guide:"Darwin",guideLine:"Evaluate both the useful trait combination and the reproductive limitation.",words:[word("sterile","bất thụ","unable to reproduce","adjective","Many zebroids are sterile."),word("pack animal","động vật thồ","an animal used to carry people or supplies","noun phrase","A strong hybrid may serve as a pack animal."),word("evidence","bằng chứng","information used to support a conclusion","noun","Scientists compare evidence before making a recommendation.")],questions:[mcq("What does sterile mean in this genetics lesson?",["Unable to reproduce","Free from every microbe","Easy to tame"],0,"Here sterile describes a reproductive limitation.","Use the context of offspring.","A sterile hybrid cannot have young."),tf("Test the natural-population claim.","A sterile hybrid can start a self-reproducing population without fertile offspring.",false,"Without reproduction, the hybrid cannot pass its genes to a new generation.","A population needs new offspring.","Sterility blocks that route."),gap("Complete the use case.","A strong animal that carries supplies is a ____ animal.",["pack","recessive","microscopic"],0,"Pack animals transport loads or riders.","Choose the work role.","It is today's second vocabulary phrase.")]},
    {day:5,title:"Can horses and zebras have babies together?",short:"Hybrid Review",image:"assets/science-winter-migration-v1.png",icon:"🔬",reward:"Grade 6 Hybrid Core",rewardIcon:"💎",story:"Horses and zebras share a genus but belong to different species. They can sometimes produce a hybrid called a zebroid. The offspring inherits a mixture of traits from both parents, but the exact combination can vary and the hybrid is usually sterile.",guide:"Darwin",guideLine:"Answer yes, then explain classification, inheritance and sterility.",words:[word("classification","sự phân loại","the organization of living things into groups","noun","Classification places related species in one genus."),word("trait combination","tổ hợp đặc điểm","a set of characteristics inherited together","noun phrase","Each hybrid has a distinctive trait combination."),word("reproductive","thuộc sinh sản","related to producing offspring","adjective","Sterility is a reproductive limitation.")],questions:[matching("Match each conclusion to its evidence.",[{left:"same genus",right:"share several major inherited traits"},{left:"different species",right:"do not normally produce fertile offspring together"},{left:"hybrid",right:"inherits traits from both parent species"}],"Classification and reproduction explain the zebroid.","Genus is the broader relationship.","The hybrid has two species as parents."),tf("Test the weekly answer.","A horse and zebra can sometimes produce a zebroid.",true,"These related species can mate and create a hybrid offspring.","The answer is not the same as being one species.","A hybrid is possible even when fertile offspring is not."),gap("Complete the reproductive note.","Most zebroids are ____ and cannot produce offspring.",["sterile","fertile","dominant"],0,"Sterile means unable to reproduce.","Choose the term from Day 4.","It is the major hybrid limitation."),mcq("Which statement best distinguishes genus from species?",["A genus contains related species; one species normally produces fertile offspring together","A species always contains several genera","Genus and species mean exactly the same thing"],0,"Genus is broader, while species is a more specific reproductive group.","Think broad then specific.","Horse and zebra share a genus but not a species."),mcq("Why can two zebroids look different from each other?",["Hybrid trait combinations can be unpredictable","One has no inherited traits","Their parents contribute no genes"],0,"The mix of traits inherited across species can vary.","Both parents contribute traits.","The exact combination is not guaranteed.")]}
